Blank the collection contact phone number on whitelabelled DPD labels
(v0.112)

The v0.111 Whitelabel toggle dashed out street/town, forced country to GB,
and sent a real postcode for routing - but still sent the real
contactDetails.telephone on the collectionDetails block. The user confirmed
by testing that the real number was still going out on the label.

DPD's telephone field is validated against ^([+]\d{1,14}|\d{0,15})$, which
accepts zero digits, so sending an empty string for telephone is valid
rather than being rejected outright. Now sends "" for telephone whenever
Whitelabel is on. contactName is deliberately left as configured for now -
only the phone number was reported as still showing through; can blank the
name too if that's wanted next.

